  <participating-org role="4" type="80">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UHI North, West and Hebrides</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UHI plays a central role in the academic and research dimensions of the project. UHI leads efforts in curriculum development, market research, tourism product development, and knowledge generation. This partnership bridges international and local expertise, ensuring that global best practices are effectively adapted to Cambodia&#x2019;s unique context. As part of its responsibilities, UHI will initiate comprehensive needs assessments in collaboration with RUPP. These assessments will inform the development of atailored curriculum that reflects baseline findings and insights gathered through community consultations.</narrative>
